<description>
# Fig 12.57b — Example of switch bounce (Scherz &amp; Monk, *PEI* 4th ed., fig 12.57 left panel, book p. 760)

**What it shows:** the book's *problem* panel that the debouncer (fig12_57a) fixes: a switch
with a 10 k pull-up to +5 V drives an AND gate input (the text: "the other input is fixed
high"), so `out = node`. The figure draws the node's "bounce" — on opening, the contact
oscillates between +5 V and 0 V instead of switching cleanly, and each edge passes straight
through the gate ("false triggering" on the book's out waveform).

**Parts:** RP 10 k pull-up, +5 V (book's values); SW1 SPST, node N → U1 AND input, V1 = the
fixed-high `1` [chosen: the figure text's "1"].

**How to use:** toggle SW1 (`Toggled` true = closed, node low). SimulIDE's switch toggles
cleanly, so the bounce is *stepped*: each `comp set` is one contact event, the way the book's
drawn bounce burst is a train of make/break events. Scope: CH0 = node N, CH1 = out.

**Results [SIMULATED]** — switch closed 200 µs, then a 5-event burst (open/close/open/close/
open, 100 µs apart), then settled open:

| node N | out | contact event |
|---|---|---|
| ≈ 0 V | ≈ 0 V | closed (rest) |
| 4.1946 V | 5.000 V | open — edge 1 @ 200 µs |
| ≈ 0 V | ≈ 0 V | closed — edge 2 @ 300 µs |
| 4.1948 V | 5.000 V | open — edge 3 @ 400 µs |
| ≈ 0 V | ≈ 0 V | closed — edge 4 @ 500 µs |
| 4.1924 V | 5.000 V | open — edge 5 @ 600 µs, stays |

**Five contact events → five output edges** (rise @ 200/400/600 µs, fall @ 300/500 µs): every
bounce of a real opening would false-trigger whatever counts this signal. Compare fig12_57a:
with the SR latch, the same actions move the output exactly once and hold.

- Node highs read 4.19 V, not 5 V: SimulIDE's AND subcircuit input loads the 10 k pull-up
  (≈ 52 kΩ effective, issue #127 family) — still a valid high (threshold 2.5 V), out = 5.000 V.
- AND output lows here sit at ≈ 0 V (its input low is 0 V; the −5 V lows of issue #127 come
  from the NAND outputs feeding it in fig12_57a).

## create-circuit skill

- Version: 1.4.1 (commit b897f9d)
- Circuit: fig12_57b_switch_bounce_example.sim1

### Limitations found while building it

- T_ logic gates are typed Subcircuit inside SimulIDE (fidelity false positive): [#134](https://github.com/jeroenwk/create-circuit/issues/134)
- SimulIDE NAND subcircuit outputs sit at -5 V when low; gate inputs load 10k pull-up nodes: [#135](https://github.com/jeroenwk/create-circuit/issues/135)
- SimulIDE switch cannot bounce; headless comp set steps one clean contact action: [#136](https://github.com/jeroenwk/create-circuit/issues/136)
</description>


